    "label": "th:sucb",
    "number": "Theorem (th:sucb)",
    "quote": "There exist constants $c,c'>0$ such that for any model $\\theta^*\\in\\Theta^{all}$ and any structure $\\Theta \\in \\Omega^{}$, the expected regret at time $n$ of the SUCB algorithm~\\citep{lattimore2014bounded} is upper-bounded as R_n^{\\text{SUCB}}(\\theta^*, \\Theta) \\leq \\sum_{i \\in \\mathcal{A}^* \\setminus \\{i^*\\}} \\frac{c\\Delta_i(\\theta^*)\\log n}{\\Psi(\\Theta_{i}^+, \\{i\\})} + c'."
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "New analysis of an existing algorithm (combines Lattimore&Munos and Azar et al.). c is unspecified constant (c_alg). SUCB uses log t so anytime."
  },
